                "end_index": 89,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "First and foremost, it is important to know that **there is no cure for the common cold**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 91,
                "end_index": 227,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Colds are caused by viruses (most commonly rhinoviruses), which means **antibiotics will not work** and should not be used to treat them"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 231,
                "end_index": 345,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, treatment focuses on relieving your specific symptoms while your immune system naturally clears the virus"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 482,
                "end_index": 713,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Fever, Sore Throat, and Body Aches\n*   **What to take:** Pain relievers and fever reducers like **acetaminophen** (Tylenol) or nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) like **ibuprofen** (Advil, Motrin) or **naproxen** (Aleve)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 801,
                "end_index": 927,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "** Aspirin use in youth during a viral illness is linked to a rare but life-threatening condition called **Reye\u2019s syndrome**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 937,
                "end_index": 1069,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Nasal Congestion (Stuffy Nose)\n*   **What to take:** \n    *   **Oral decongestants** like pseudoephedrine (Sudafed) or phenylephrine"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1205,
                "end_index": 1265,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Nasal decongestant sprays** like oxymetazoline (Afrin)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1268,
                "end_index": 1386,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **\u26a0\ufe0f Critical Safety Warning:** Do not use nasal decongestant sprays for more than **3 to 5 consecutive days**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1538,
                "end_index": 1618,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Instead, use safe **saline nasal sprays or rinses** to keep nasal passages moist"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1628,
                "end_index": 1757,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Cough\n*   **What to take:** \n    *   For a dry, hacking cough: A **cough suppressant** like dextromethorphan (Robitussin, Delsym)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1763,
                "end_index": 1901,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   For a wet, mucus-filled cough: An **expectorant** like guaifenesin (Mucinex), which helps thin and loosen mucus so you can cough it up"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1903,
                "end_index": 2053,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Natural Alternative:** For adults and children older than 1 year, **honey** is a highly effective, clinically supported remedy to soothe a cough"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2055,
                "end_index": 2141,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*(Never give honey to infants under 1 year of age due to the risk of infant botulism)*"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2151,
                "end_index": 2263,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Runny Nose and Sneezing\n*   **What to take:** Antihistamines like diphenhydramine (Benadryl) or chlorpheniramine"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2265,
                "end_index": 2359,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Older antihistamines can help dry up a runny nose, but they often cause significant drowsiness"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2446,
                "end_index": 2586,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Watch Out for \"Double Dosing\":** Many over-the-counter (OTC) cold products are marketed as \"multi-symptom\" or \"all-in-one\" medications"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2588,
                "end_index": 2672,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "These often contain a mixture of acetaminophen, a decongestant, and an antihistamine"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2674,
                "end_index": 2832,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "If you take a multi-symptom medication *and* a separate dose of Tylenol, you could accidentally overdose on acetaminophen, which can cause severe liver damage"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2834,
                "end_index": 2894,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Always read the \"Active Ingredients\" on the Drug Facts label"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2896,
                "end_index": 3121,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Pediatric Safety:** The FDA strongly advises **against** giving OTC cough and cold medications to infants and young children (especially those under 4 years old) due to the risk of serious, life-threatening side effects"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3123,
                "end_index": 3255,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "For children, safe supportive care includes a cool-mist humidifier, saline nasal drops, gentle bulb suctioning, and plenty of fluids"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3257,
                "end_index": 3340,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   **Non-Medicinal Support:** Do not underestimate the power of rest and hydration"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3342,
                "end_index": 3435,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Drinking plenty of water, warm tea, or clear broths helps thin mucus and prevents dehydration"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3438,
                "end_index": 3514,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "### When to See a Doctor\nMost colds resolve on their own within 7 to 10 days"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3516,
                "end_index": 3643,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "However, you should consult a healthcare provider if you experience:\n*   Difficulty breathing, wheezing, or shortness of breath"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                4
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3645,
                "end_index": 3733,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   A high fever that lasts longer than 3\u20134 days or does not respond to fever reducers"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3782,
                "end_index": 3918,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "*   Symptoms that last longer than 10 to 14 days without any improvement, or symptoms that start to get better but suddenly worsen again"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
          ],
